// JXL - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// JPEG XL has two container forms. The naked codestream starts with
// FF 0A; the container form is ISOBMFF and starts with a `JXL `
// signature box, which is why this file does not start with ftyp and
// why the checker is told which box it is allowed to see first.
//
// Hello World! is in a `free` box, which is this format's own
// skip space and the same role a PNG tEXt chunk plays.
//
// jxl: 40 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 00 00 00 14 4A 58 4C 20 00 00 00 0C 4A 58 4C 20 |....JXL ....JXL |   <- 0000
// 0D 0A 87 0A 00 00 00 14 66 72 65 65 48 65 6C 6C |........freeHell|   <- 0010
// 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21                         |o World!|   <- 0020
